  "floor_binding_conclusion": "ASYMMETRIC: the floor bound HARD on w_F (flux confidence) -- every fold wants w_F near 0 (0.05, the smallest nonzero grid step), well below the old 0.15 floor. It did NOT bind on w_C (consensus) in the direction of holding it down -- every fold wants w_C substantially ABOVE 0.15 (0.35-0.6), i.e. 0.15 was actually far LOWER than what the objective prefers for consensus. Forcing w_F up to its 0.15 minimum (which the objective does not want at all) consumed weight budget, and the remaining 0.85 split between w_C and w_P within the floor-constrained search space landed at 0.15/0.70 as the best AVAILABLE combination under that restriction -- not because w_C wanted to be low, but because the floor-constrained grid never explored the true unconstrained preference (high w_C, near-zero w_F, moderate w_P). CONCLUSION: the floor was actively constraining the result, and the true unconstrained preference is consensus-dominant, not perturbation-dominant, contrary to what (0.15,0.15,0.70) suggests.",
